// spurious_correlation.ivl -- a genuinely spurious alarm.
// Two variables are kept equal (y == x), and the program guards the
// division with (x - y != 0).  Concretely the guard can never be true, so
// the division is unreachable and nothing ever crashes.  The non-
// relational interval domain, however, tracks x and y independently as
// Top, so on the "then" edge it cannot narrow either of them and reports a
// *possible* division by zero.  Over any bounded input region the
// exhaustive checker finds zero concrete crashes: this alarm is the
// precision boundary, not a real bug.
input var x;
var y = x;
if (x - y != 0) {
    var z = 1 / (x - y);
}
